    <code code="10154-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Chief complaint Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Chief Complaint</title>
    <text><paragraph>Neurology evaluation of lifelong spells and headache after a head injury. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mrs. Tubman is seen two weeks after her primary care visit for headaches on most days and sudden sleep spells since a severe head injury in her early teens. She stopped daily ibuprofen at that visit. Her headaches were worse for the first several days and have eased since; she has used acetaminophen on no more than 2 days a week and is keeping a headache diary. The spells continue several times a day, often while seated in conversation or at meetings, and end after a few minutes; she wakes and picks up where she left off. Witnesses have described no stiffening, jerking, lip-smacking, tongue biting, or incontinence, and she is not confused afterward. She has never had sudden weakness with laughter or strong emotion. She does not drive. She does not want medicine that makes her duller. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Spells</td><td>Several a day, mostly while seated; last a few minutes and end abruptly</td></tr><tr><td>Witnessed features</td><td>No stiffening, jerking, automatisms, tongue biting, incontinence, or confusion afterward</td></tr><tr><td>Cataplexy</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Headache since stopping ibuprofen</td><td>Worse for several days, then easing</td></tr><tr><td>Acute medicine</td><td>Acetaminophen on no more than 2 days a week; no ibuprofen</td></tr><tr><td>Driving</td><td>Does not drive</td></tr><tr><td>Patient preference</td><td>No sedating medicine</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

